research/audit/wave11-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-taylor-peano-remainder.log-4755-research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:14:{"id":"cor-taylor-lagrange-and-cauchy-remainders","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://mathworld.wolfram.com/SchloemilchRemainder.html","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_taylor.html"],"rationale":"The sources give the Lagrange and Cauchy forms as the corresponding special cases of Taylor's remainder. The item packages both in one corollary under its parent theorem's relative-interval conventions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-09"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-taylor-peano-remainder.log:4756:research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:15:{"id":"thm-taylor-peano-remainder","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.drexel.edu/~tolya/Lagrange%20remainder.pdf"],"rationale":"Grinshpan's university Real Analysis note states the Peano form under n-times differentiability at the expansion point, with remainder o((x-a)^n), matching the item's hypothesis, quantifier, and direction. The inductive quotient proof is local.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-10"}
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-taylor-peano-remainder.log:4757:research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl:16:{"id":"cor-taylor-remainder-bound","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://www.math.drexel.edu/~tolya/Lagrange%20remainder.pdf"],"rationale":"Grinshpan's university Real Analysis note states the Lagrange remainder formula under the corresponding derivative hypotheses; taking the displayed derivative value at the intermediate point under the uniform bound gives exactly M|x-a|^{n+1}/(n+1)!. The repository's proof is a direct local application of its preceding remainder theorem.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-10"}
