research/audit/wave11-dispatch/certifier-a6-thm-taylor-peano-remainder.log-10390-title: "The chain rule, in one line from Carathéodory: if $g$ is differentiable at $c$ and $f$ is differentiable at $g(c)$, then $f \\circ g$ is differentiable at $c$ with $(f \\circ g)'(c) = f'(g(c))\\,g'(c)$"
